abstract: >
  Raw benchmark data (10 repeated runs per system), relationship inventories,
  model-attributed eager-load counts, a provenance record, benchmark harness code
  and analysis scripts for a PhD thesis proposing a design-time decision model:
  a null-share check followed by a statistical decision rule (a two-tailed
  one-sample t-test over repeated per-relationship cold/warm cache access
  measurements) for determining which Eloquent/ORM relationships are worth
  caching before a caching layer is implemented. Applied to three separately
  deployed Laravel/Eloquent systems: iTeams, Khairat Kematian, and the Vehicle
  Booking System (VBS).
